  "title": "Mott",
  "country": "UK",
  "released": "1973-07-00",
  "notes": "This is the original UK release in matt gatefold cover, on plain orange CBS labels.\n• This album has a Unipak cover [disc access from the inside] with only one card layer for the die-cut front flap, where the acetate sheet is glued to an additional tab.\nTop-opening lyrics/credits inner sleeve with a thumb cut-out, 'Patent No. 1,125,555', 'CBS Records 28-30 Theobalds Road London WC 1', 'Made In Great Britain.' and 'P' on side B. \nFirst catalogue number on cover, 2nd on labels.\nSome copies may contain a sticker on front cover reading: \"featuring hit single HONALOOCHIE BOOGIE\".\n\nRecorded at Air London Studios, and EMI Abbey Road - February through April 1973.\n\n℗ 1973 CBS Inc.\n\nB2 appears as:\n• \"Ballad Of Mott The Hoople (March 26, 1972-Zurich)\" on cover;\n• \"Ballad Of Mott (March 26th 1972, Zurich) (I. Hunter/O. Watts/M. Ralphs/Buffin/V. Allen)\" on label;\n• \"Ballad Of Mott (March 26th 1972 Zurich) (Ian Hunter/Buffin/Overend Watts/Mick Ralphs)\" on lyrics inner sleeve.\nB3[b] appears on cover as \"El Camino Dolo Roso\", but as \"El Comino Dolo Roso\" on label [The painful path vs. the painful cumin].\n\n\"A Sane Revolution\" from \"The Complete Poems of [a648014]\" [Poem on cover rear]\nCBS is a Trademark of the Columbia Broadcasting System Inc., U.S.A.\nUnipak by Shorewood Packaging Co. Ltd., England.\nTyp. Tina Young [inner sleeve]\nMade In England [labels]\n\nPublished by Island Music-UK, Ackee Music Inc. USA\n\nRunouts are stamped. This submission includes both the first [A1/B1] and the second [A1/B2] master cut.",
  "released_formatted": "Jul 1973",
